        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/id": "3d06c7b2-cab2-5c7e-a403-4af7390c868f",
        ":question/problem": "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/28/28da4f28a9c39d920981931bc1f5244ed8c7b3ee95a4f03b4117cf9571df87a3.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "![Completed vector route](images/ba/ba64fc7f92d4394d5830087812d4046c85ee2a171d65d4686f6b2cdf85aee8b4.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $1$ square right. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square right. Thus $OX=1|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $4$ squares left and $4$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares right and $2$ squares up. Thus $XC=2|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-2\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=1$ and $\\mu=-2$."
      }
    }
