        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/id": "93a0c8ae-a9f6-5bb5-a4ae-ea1b4ffe8a11",
        ":question/problem": "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/df/dfbb1c2b7b6a9d0526e917a12349300a4ffff7178f33d63d0dcfe04e1df2fc2b.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "![Completed vector route](images/f7/f7bd99f24d33518bd2ec1e6e901ae9cafafb57b3e25d7dd8b8d0451b4959598d.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $2$ squares right and $2$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square up. Thus $OX=2|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-2\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $1$ square left. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares left. Thus $XC=\\frac{1}{2}|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-2\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\mu=-2$."
